# @moeru/eventa (pulled in by the merged airi packages under src/airi) declares an OPTIONAL peer on
# @tauri-apps/api >= 2, for its Tauri transport. amica ships a Tauri v1 desktop shell (src-tauri/,
# and src/components/vrmViewer.tsx imports "@tauri-apps/api/tauri" — the v1 module path, which v2
# renamed to /core). So the two cannot be satisfied at once, and npm refuses the whole install:
# without this flag `npm install` and `npm ci` both fail outright and the front end cannot be built.
#
# Relaxing it is correct rather than a workaround: the peer is optional, and the web build uses
# NEITHER side of it — eventa's Tauri transport is not reachable from any route we ship, and the
# Tauri v1 API is only used by the desktop shell, which pins its own v1 through @tauri-apps/cli.
# Upgrading @tauri-apps/api to v2 instead would break that shell's import path with no Rust-side
# upgrade to match.
#
# This is read by `npm ci` in CI too, so the lockfile resolves identically there.
legacy-peer-deps=true
